Task: FR-9 (PRD.md §4.2) — unit test forcing each of the three traffic-risk preconditions
and asserting traffic_risk_source reports the correct tier each time.

REAL DISCREPANCY FOUND (flagged for human review): both README.md ("now has three tiers,
checked in order: live -> personal -> generic") and PRD.md's own FR-9 wording describe THREE
traffic-risk tiers. Reading _get_traffic_risk directly shows FOUR tiers actually exist: live
-> zone (_get_traffic_risk_by_zone -- a rounded lat/lon grid cell + hour combination,
requiring >=ZONE_MIN_SAMPLES=3 same-zone-same-hour trips) -> personal (_is_peak_hour,
hour-of-day only, >=5 total trips) -> generic. The "zone" tier is real, working code that
neither README.md nor PRD.md currently document. This is the second documentation-vs-code
gap found this loop (after the stale TODO section PRD.md's own status note already flags) --
recommend PRD.md §4.2 FR-9 and README.md's traffic section both get updated to describe 4
tiers, not 3. NOT fixing README.md/PRD.md wording in this iteration per ralph/PROMPT.md's
guardrail (doc updates are their own task, not a side effect of a test-writing task) --
flagging here for a human or a future dedicated task to act on.

Wrote app/src/main/python/tests/test_smart_score_traffic_risk.py, 5 tests covering all 4 real
tiers (more thorough than the 3-tier task wording, to match actual behavior):
1. Generic, off-peak hour (10) -> low risk.
2. Generic, peak hour (12, lunch window) -> high risk.
3. Personal tier activates once >=5 total trips exist (4 fast trips at hour 8, 1 slow at hour
   17, no lat/lon so zone can never trigger) -> correctly identifies hour 17 as high-risk
   relative to the driver's own overall average.
4. Zone tier overrides personal when same-zone-same-hour data exists (3 slow trips in one
   zone at hour 9 + 1 faster same-zone trip at a different hour, PLUS 5 unrelated trips that
   would satisfy the personal tier on their own) -> source is "zone", not "personal",
   confirming real priority ordering, not just "only data present."
5. Live tier overrides zone AND personal when a fresh reading exists (same zone fixture as
   test 4, plus record_live_traffic_delay) -> source is "live".

